A||N||6||308||Why is my Volt light coming on faint||||5||
Z||000000||308||07-28-2001||12:43 AM||||I have an 87 (not sure if it's gt or se) becasue it's a 308 kit. anyway the volt battery light is on very light. during the day you can bairly see it but at night you can see it.  I had the Alt. and the battery checked. Both check out o.k. Is this a common problem and what might cause this. Thanks LArry||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||07-28-2001||12:52 AM||||Usually means that the alternator is on its way out.||||reg||1
Z||000002||SteveJ||07-28-2001||07:28 AM||||The alternator is still producing electricity but not enough. Hence the glow. Your battery is slowly discharging. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||starfighter007@msn.com||07-28-2001||04:27 PM||||you have a bad diode in your alternator.If it were me I would just replace the alternator with a rebuilt one before you are left stranded some where with a dead battery.||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||07-28-2001||04:34 PM||||one other possibility is that something else is grounding thru this light. I've seen the same thing on a car where the stereo was not grounded properly and it used the oil press light for a grnd. (don't know how or why, it just did) when he ran a good grnd to the case of the stereo it stopped illuminating the op light.It' a possibility, if you are sure the alt & batt are ok.||||reg||1
Z||000005||308||07-28-2001||06:07 PM||||Thanks for all of the reply's The reply about the ground and the radio never thought of that, but this just happend about 3 weeks ago. and the radio has been in for a long time, Looks like I will be buying and alternator<BR>"boy it sucks living in an Apartment gotta pay someone to put in a Alternator. ||||reg||1
